 "notModeled": [
  "analog input, PGA, burn-out sources, bias voltage, system monitors (MUXCAL), internal reference, reference select, IDACs (stored only)",
  "GPIOs on the analog pins (GPIOCFG/GPIODIR/GPIODAT stored only; the pins are analog in the model)",
  "offset/gain calibration commands (SYSOCAL, SYSGCAL, SELFOCAL) and the OFC/FSC correction of the result (registers stored only)",
  "conversion time is the first conversion after reset / START high / WAKEUP (Table 10); SYNC/MUX0-write and subsequent conversions are slightly shorter; internal 4.096 MHz oscillator (external CLK scales it; the CLK pin is not used)",
  "writes to the first four registers (00h-03h) restart the conversion like SYNC (datasheet); not modeled",
  "SLEEP completes the ongoing conversion before power-down; with START low or in power-down only RDATA, RDATAC, SDATAC, WAKEUP and NOP work (all commands work in the model)",
  "START pin pulse single conversions (device powers down after each conversion when START is low): modeled as conversions only while START is high",
  "SDATAC mode (results not loaded onto DOUT automatically) and RDATAC taking effect at the next DRDY; any command during an RREG reply is ignored (datasheet)",
  "DRDY is forced high by the first SCLK falling edge after it falls, even with CS high (modeled: cleared on result read); tPWH high pulse when the data are not read",
  "DOUT/DRDY after the 16 data bits: forced high by the next SCLK rising edge when DRDY MODE = 1 (modeled idle 1 in both modes)",
  "RREG count wrapping past the last register; the restricted command F1h; SPI timeout after 64 conversion cycles",
  "RESET command / pin recovery time (0.6 ms) and the 2^16-clock power-on reset",
  "tDOPD is 50 ns at DVDD <= 3.6 V (180 ns above)"
 ],
